_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 32
---
order: 32
---
short_label: VI.32
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two triangles having two sides proportional to two sides are placed together at one angle so that their corresponding sides are also parallel, then the remaining sides of the triangles are in a straight line.
----
proof:

Let *ABC* and *DCE* be two triangles having the two sides *AB* and *AC* proportional to the two sides *DC* and *DE,* so that *AB* is to *AC* as *DC* is to *DE,* and *AB* parallel to *DC,* and *AC* parallel to *DE.*

I say that *BC* is in a straight line with *CE.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="370" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.32 diagram" src="propVI32.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
